            "review_title": "Review at Soma Art Cafe",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nHidden Gem in D2\nApr 2019 • Friends\nBrunch at Soma Art Lounge was a sheer delight. Inside the decor is minimalist, smart and stylish, the owner is very welcoming and friendly and the breakfast was hot and tasty. The free flow Mimosas were very refreshing too. We went with friends who also enjoyed their food, for example one friend had the tuna sandwiches and another friend the cheese and tomato bagel. Most of us had various breakfasts however. My bacon was crispy, as requested, the sausage well cooked all over and pleasant, the eggs well cooked - sunny side up but sealed properly on top so that they weren't slimy, and the toast was brown for once and actually looked and tasted like toast. We have found that most toast in the city is an under cooked white colour with a stale texture, due to being under toasted. But here in Soma it is proper western golden brown toast which is such a treat. The tomatoes were also grilled well. We will definitely be back soon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 3, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
