            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_5",
            "review_title": "Review at Soma Art Cafe",
            "review_text": "philawesomer\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam26 contributions\n0\nQuiet, cozy... most of the time.\nMar 2019 • Solo\nI don't want to share Soma with anyone. This quiet, not-so-secret cafe in District 2, is almost always empty. That’s why I like it. The people running Soma don’t play loud music, they don’t loom over you expecting you to order from the bar… which you should, by the way. Their coffee is made with love and their cocktails aren’t fancy, but they’re good and fairly priced. They don’t have any food, which is disappointing, but (in my experience) they don’t mind if you bring snacks.\n\nBut, when there’s an event, Soma comes alive with people. It’s crowded, loud, and marvelous. They host art exhibitions, dancing nights, drag shows, open mic nights, and so many events that you can’t see them all. True, I visit Soma to work in peace and quiet, but I can also go there to be part of the event scene of Saigon. Soma does it all.\n\nGo to Soma--just not when I’m there. I like my peace and quiet. :)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 3, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
